WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:04.423
- [Eric] Yep, that's me.

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:06.630
You're probably wondering how I ended up here,

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:07.863
let's take a step back.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.563
My name is Eric and I grew up here,

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:13.403
^birthplace of La Croix sparkling water.

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:15.393
Seltzer is in my blood.

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:19.653
So today, I'm gonna try as many flavors as I can.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:22.650
It's a lot of seltzer to try so I'm gonna have

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:25.150
some friends help me out and select our favorites.

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:28.370
After I've tried them all we're gonna combine all 70

00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:30.623
to make the world's first mega-seltzer.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:32.493
First up, Polar.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:34.550
^- I hated seltzer water my whole life

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:37.993
^and then dated somebody who loved Polar.

00:00:38.186 --> 00:00:40.936
(popping sounds)

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:48.880
^- I don't like to do seltzer with straws.

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:52.000
^I think you lose the carbonation in the straw

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:54.323
on the way to your mouth, right?

00:00:54.675 --> 00:00:57.425
(popping sounds)

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:01.633
- Yeah, that's good, I'm into that.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:03.920
- I'm eating seltzer for lunch.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:06.833
- Up next, Hal's.

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:09.090
How are you related to the company?

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:10.537
^Second cousin--

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:13.730
^- I wish I could say I was, like, the CEO and owner,

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:17.130
but I get no profit from how many

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:18.630
Hal's seltzer waters are sold.

00:01:18.844 --> 00:01:21.594
(popping sounds)

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:26.263
I wonder what intern was like, "Okay,

00:01:26.407 --> 00:01:29.067
"I have an idea, a coffee-flavored water."

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:34.570
I mean, it's not bad, it's not bad.

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:35.670
- It's not bad, right?

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:36.683
- It's not bad.

00:01:36.683 --> 00:01:38.290
I'm kinda mad about that, actually.

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:40.390
It tastes a little bit like when you

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:42.840
have consumed an iced coffee and,

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:45.070
like, the ice is melted and it's just,

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:48.030
like, the watery flavor down at the bottom,

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:49.653
that's a little bit what it tastes like.

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:52.123
- Up next, Bubly.

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:54.073
Bubly.

00:01:54.073 --> 00:01:54.906
- Bubly.

00:01:54.906 --> 00:01:55.739
- No, I think it's Bubly.

00:01:55.739 --> 00:01:59.970
^- It says no calories, no sweeteners, all smiles,

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:02.340
^and as a woman I find that offensive

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:05.420
because I don't like anybody telling me to smile,

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:07.053
especially not my seltzer.

00:02:07.071 --> 00:02:09.821
(popping sounds)

00:02:10.056 --> 00:02:12.273
- I'm just trying to hold back so many burps.

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:15.410
- It's probably gonna be really unpleasant

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:18.030
coming out of your mouth and out of your butt later

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:20.710
because I bet you're gonna get a lot of farts.

00:02:20.710 --> 00:02:23.460
(popping sounds)

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:25.630
- Do you think Michael Buble is a brand ambassador for this?

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:26.780
- I mean, he should be.

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:28.433
If he isn't, they're idiots.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:33.333
I mean, smooth jazz, smooth sparkling water.

00:02:33.797 --> 00:02:34.997
- Is he a jazz musician?

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:38.040
- Doesn't he play, like, the jazz clarinet or something?

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:40.260
Or no, am I getting him confused with someone.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:41.093
- Kenny G?

00:02:41.210 --> 00:02:42.510
- I'm thinking of Kenny G.

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:46.223
- Next up is Spindrift.

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:49.130
This is made with real fruit as opposed

00:02:49.130 --> 00:02:50.680
to being an essence with fruit.

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:53.063
^I still don't know what essence means.

00:02:53.064 --> 00:02:55.814
(popping sounds)

00:02:58.300 --> 00:02:59.283
Ten calories?

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:02.253
This is the most caloric seltzer we've had yet.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:05.273
Up next, Adirondack.

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:08.070
^- I immediately was brought back to

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:09.963
^when I get sick and I get medicine.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.160
- I mean, I feel sick but I think

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:11.993
it's for a different reason.

00:03:11.993 --> 00:03:13.548
(popping sounds)

00:03:13.548 --> 00:03:15.450
(Eric burping)

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:17.200
- I can't work in these conditions.

00:03:17.379 --> 00:03:20.129
(popping sounds)

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:24.623
- Up next, 365.

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:27.480
So we are starting with your favorite flavor.

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:30.423
- Yes, which is a lack of flavor.

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:33.420
(popping sounds)

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:37.193
- [Eric] Next up is Vintage, 17 left.

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:39.000
- You'll see this when you open it,

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:40.533
it's gonna be substantial.

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:42.060
- You think it'll erupt?

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:43.789
- You gotta be careful.

00:03:43.789 --> 00:03:45.649
(popping sounds)

00:03:45.649 --> 00:03:46.869
(Eric burping)

00:03:46.869 --> 00:03:47.869
- Excuse me.

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:51.693
Up next, La Croix, only 14 more to go.

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:53.490
- I always called it La Croix

00:03:54.140 --> 00:03:56.630
^because that's the correct pronunciation,

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:58.930
but then I understand it's based on the river,

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:01.370
which the locals call La Croix, I guess.

00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:02.310
Whatever, it doesn't matter.

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:03.893
- Alright, hope you're thirsty.

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:06.873
- Oh, honey, oh, me.

00:04:06.967 --> 00:04:09.717
(popping sounds)

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:13.793
- So why is it called pamplemousse,

00:04:13.793 --> 00:04:15.243
is that how you pronounce it?

00:04:15.252 --> 00:04:16.366
- Pamplemousse?

00:04:16.366 --> 00:04:18.116
^I mean, it's French for grapefruit.

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:21.830
- It's French, I didn't know that.

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:23.710
- Okay, so as part of my, like,

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:26.333
La Croix boy identity I've realized something.

00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:28.047
I feel like there's actually--

00:04:28.113 --> 00:04:31.280
(overlapping talking)

00:04:38.070 --> 00:04:38.903
- Totally.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:39.753
- Right?

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:42.653
- [Eric] And now the grand finale, Schweppes,

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:44.453
only four more to taste.

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:46.437
- I am kind of a lukewarm on seltzer

00:04:46.437 --> 00:04:48.523
^only because it makes me gassy.

00:04:48.722 --> 00:04:50.789
(popping sounds)

00:04:50.789 --> 00:04:53.039
- I've waited what feels like years for this.

00:04:53.070 --> 00:04:54.870
I feel greasy, I'm kind of sweating.

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:56.323
Ironically I'm thirsty.

00:04:56.740 --> 00:04:57.573
Cheers.

00:04:57.573 --> 00:04:58.406
- Cheers.

00:05:03.254 --> 00:05:07.337
(celebratory instrumental music)

00:05:11.336 --> 00:05:12.490
- Well, we're not quite done.

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:14.370
As promised, we are going to attempt

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:16.510
something that has never been done before.

00:05:16.530 --> 00:05:18.740
We are going to combine all 70 seltzers,

00:05:18.740 --> 00:05:20.740
which I just drank, into a big vat

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:23.080
and create the world's first mega-seltzer.

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:26.580
(instrumental rock music)

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:35.760
- It's a little off-white, which I love.

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:38.813
- It's kind of like a very pale Rose.

00:05:43.364 --> 00:05:44.614
- There's a lot going on.

00:05:47.970 --> 00:05:48.803
- I don't hate it.

00:05:48.803 --> 00:05:50.110
- It's just weird, it's just weird.

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:51.833
- I see things floating in there.

00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:54.320
- It's perplexing.

00:05:56.610 --> 00:05:57.860
- [Eric] So there you have it.

00:05:57.860 --> 00:06:00.120
We tried every seltzer we could get our hands on

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:03.263
and we combined every seltzer we could get our hands on,

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:06.533
and now, now I gotta pee.

00:06:06.671 --> 00:06:10.171
(instrumental rock music)

